{"kind":"request","text":"Installed-release listing: live reads refused. Child of 521f57a1 (landed Main d73b53c9, check 08542cf6).\n\nObserved 06:33 to 06:36, CLI at d73b53c9 from the planner's deploy worktree, each Worker's operator home as DAP_HOME, sequence inventory then applications:\n- dap-grow: manifest sha256:902ac75b… (11 scopes); report sha256:d2034159…, 0 applications, 11 errors, every scope \"forbidden\", exit 1.\n- dap-lending: manifest sha256:cd67ae0a… (8 scopes); report sha256:e4bec7fe…, 0 applications, 8 errors, every scope \"forbidden\", exit 1.\n- dap-demo: inventory refused (\"No configured room Directory\"); applications refused, configuration-unavailable. The dap-demo operator home has no repository; the planner owns that gap.\nEvidence read-only with SHA256SUMS at /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-27-release-listing-run-0630 (manifests, reports, logs; scope references and fixed reasons only).\n\nThe same operator read all 11 dap-grow scopes through the sweep path at 04:56 (tail-0450.json). The listing's signed-only summary GET without a session is refused by both hosts; the sweep's session plus signed read is admitted. So the landed command cannot produce a complete report against any live Worker, and dap-demo and dap-lending stay held on their 1b45fb0e deploys.\n\nDeliver, in order:\n1. From source at d73b53c9, state which authorization the host's summary path requires for an operator's signed read without a session, and why the sweep's read passes. No live read is needed for this step; the planner's reports are the observation.\n2. A listing that reads with the operator's existing session path, qualified the way the sweep is (the session acquisition is the operator's own and is named in the note and in docs/deploy.md as the one request beyond the summary GET), unless step 1 shows the host already admits signed operator reads under a configuration the planner lacks; then name the configuration instead. Ruling 2dc765ac is amended to